SIEM Dashboards for Data Visualization

SIEM tools create dashboards that present security information in an easy-to-understand format, similar to how weather apps display data.
These dashboards use charts, graphs, and tables to visualize security data, helping analysts quickly identify patterns and trends.
Practical Application of SIEM Dashboards

Security analysts use dashboards to gather information about alerts, such as suspicious login attempts, by reviewing visual representations of timelines, locations, and activity times.
This allows for rapid assessment of suspicious activity, as demonstrated by an example of 500 login attempts from unusual locations and times for a single account.
Customization and Metrics

SIEM dashboards provide a comprehensive summary of security data and can be customized to display specific metrics relevant to different organizational members.
Metrics, such as response time and failure rate, are key technical attributes used to assess software application performance, and dashboards can be tailored to monitor everyday business operations like network traffic volume.
